// Q-165 The guide's signup writes into a tenant that already exists: `with_tenant` makes a tenant or enters one, so anyone who signs up a taken name runs that code in its database
// mode: script
// script: steps.sh
// open-when: the sample checks for an existing tenant: no
// fixed-when: the sample checks for an existing tenant: yes
// From FEEDBACK20.md §Q-165 (found on 9e8c2fb). The program is the guide's, under "Many tenants".

tenant_from("example.com")
db.open("data/{tenant}.db")
db.migrate()

route POST /signup { form: { name: str } } {
    with_tenant(name, () => db.exec("insert into settings (plan) values ('free')"))
    "made " + name
}
route GET /plans = db.query("select plan from settings")
